{"id":"G0125","name":"HAFNIUM","aliases":["Operation Exchange Marauder","Silk Typhoon"],"url":"https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0125","summary":"HAFNIUM is a likely state-sponsored cyber espionage group operating out of China that has been active since at least January 2021. HAFNIUM primarily targets entities in the US across a number of industry sectors, including infectious disease researchers, law firms, higher education institutions, defense contractors, policy think tanks, and NGOs. HAFNIUM has targeted remote management tools and cloud software for intial access and has demonstrated an ability to quickly operationalize exploits for identified vulnerabilities in edge devices.","summaryCites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"},{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"},{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}],"procedures":[{"id":"T1078.003","text":"HAFNIUM has used the NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM account to create files on Exchange servers.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye Exchange Zero Days March 2021","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2021/03/detection-response-to-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities.html"}]},{"id":"T1078.004","text":"HAFNIUM has abused service principals in compromised environments to enable data exfiltration.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1218.011","text":"HAFNIUM has used `rundll32` to load malicious DLLs.","cites":[{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"}]},{"id":"T1564.001","text":"HAFNIUM has hidden files on a compromised host.","cites":[{"name":"Rapid7 HAFNIUM Mar 2021","url":"https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2021/03/23/defending-against-the-zero-day-analyzing-attacker-behavior-post-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange/"}]},{"id":"T1685.005","text":"HAFNIUM has cleared actor-performed actions from logs.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1589.002","text":"HAFNIUM has collected e-mail addresses for users they intended to target.","cites":[{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"}]},{"id":"T1590","text":"HAFNIUM gathered the fully qualified domain names (FQDNs) for targeted Exchange servers in the victim's environment.","cites":[{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"}]},{"id":"T1590.005","text":"HAFNIUM has obtained IP addresses for publicly-accessible Exchange servers.","cites":[{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"}]},{"id":"T1592.004","text":"HAFNIUM has interacted with Office 365 tenants to gather details regarding target's environments.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"}]},{"id":"T1593.003","text":"HAFNIUM has discovered leaked corporate credentials on public repositories including GitHub.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1583.003","text":"HAFNIUM has operated from leased virtual private servers (VPS) in the United States.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"}]},{"id":"T1583.005","text":"HAFNIUM has incorporated leased devices into covert networks to obfuscate communications.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1583.006","text":"HAFNIUM has acquired web services for use in C2 and exfiltration.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"}]},{"id":"T1584.005","text":"HAFNIUM has used compromised devices in covert networks to obfuscate communications.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1190","text":"HAFNIUM has exploited multiple vulnerabilities to compromise edge devices and on-premises versions of Microsoft Exchange Server.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"},{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"},{"name":"FireEye Exchange Zero Days March 2021","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2021/03/detection-response-to-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities.html"}]},{"id":"T1199","text":"HAFNIUM has used stolen API keys and credentials associated with privilege access management (PAM), cloud app providers, and cloud data management companies to access downstream customer environments.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1059.001","text":"HAFNIUM has used the Exchange Power Shell module `Set-OabVirtualDirectoryPowerShell` to export mailbox data.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"},{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"}]},{"id":"T1059.003","text":"HAFNIUM has used `cmd.exe` to execute commands on the victim's machine.","cites":[{"name":"Rapid7 HAFNIUM Mar 2021","url":"https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2021/03/23/defending-against-the-zero-day-analyzing-attacker-behavior-post-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange/"}]},{"id":"T1098","text":"HAFNIUM has granted privileges to domain accounts and reset the password for default admin accounts.","cites":[{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"},{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1136.002","text":"HAFNIUM has created domain accounts.","cites":[{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"},{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1505.003","text":"HAFNIUM has deployed multiple web shells on compromised servers including SIMPLESEESHARP, SPORTSBALL, China Chopper, and ASPXSpy.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"},{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"},{"name":"FireEye Exchange Zero Days March 2021","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2021/03/detection-response-to-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities.html"}]},{"id":"T1068","text":"HAFNIUM has targeted unpatched applications to elevate access in targeted organizations.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1003.001","text":"HAFNIUM has used `procdump` to dump the LSASS process memory.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"},{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"},{"name":"Rapid7 HAFNIUM Mar 2021","url":"https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2021/03/23/defending-against-the-zero-day-analyzing-attacker-behavior-post-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange/"}]},{"id":"T1003.003","text":"HAFNIUM has stolen copies of the Active Directory database (NTDS.DIT).","cites":[{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"},{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1110.003","text":"HAFNIUM has gained initial access through password spray attacks.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1555.006","text":"HAFNIUM has moved laterally from on-premises environments to steal passwords from Azure key vaults.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1016","text":"HAFNIUM has collected IP information via IPInfo.","cites":[{"name":"Rapid7 HAFNIUM Mar 2021","url":"https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2021/03/23/defending-against-the-zero-day-analyzing-attacker-behavior-post-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange/"}]},{"id":"T1016.001","text":"HAFNIUM has checked for network connectivity from a compromised host using `ping`, including attempts to contact `google[.]com`.","cites":[{"name":"Rapid7 HAFNIUM Mar 2021","url":"https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2021/03/23/defending-against-the-zero-day-analyzing-attacker-behavior-post-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange/"}]},{"id":"T1018","text":"HAFNIUM has enumerated domain controllers using `net group \"Domain computers\"` and `nltest /dclist`.","cites":[{"name":"Rapid7 HAFNIUM Mar 2021","url":"https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2021/03/23/defending-against-the-zero-day-analyzing-attacker-behavior-post-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange/"}]},{"id":"T1033","text":"HAFNIUM has used `whoami` to gather user information.","cites":[{"name":"Rapid7 HAFNIUM Mar 2021","url":"https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2021/03/23/defending-against-the-zero-day-analyzing-attacker-behavior-post-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange/"}]},{"id":"T1057","text":"HAFNIUM has used `tasklist` to enumerate processes.","cites":[{"name":"Rapid7 HAFNIUM Mar 2021","url":"https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2021/03/23/defending-against-the-zero-day-analyzing-attacker-behavior-post-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange/"}]},{"id":"T1083","text":"HAFNIUM has searched file contents on a compromised host.","cites":[{"name":"Rapid7 HAFNIUM Mar 2021","url":"https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2021/03/23/defending-against-the-zero-day-analyzing-attacker-behavior-post-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange/"}]},{"id":"T1550.001","text":"HAFNIUM has abused service principals with administrative permissions for data exfiltration.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1005","text":"HAFNIUM has collected data and files from a compromised machine.","cites":[{"name":"Rapid7 HAFNIUM Mar 2021","url":"https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2021/03/23/defending-against-the-zero-day-analyzing-attacker-behavior-post-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange/"},{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1114.002","text":"HAFNIUM has used web shells and MSGraph to export mailbox data.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"},{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"},{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1119","text":"HAFNIUM has used MSGraph to exfiltrate data from email, OneDrive, and SharePoint.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1213.002","text":"HAFNIUM has abused compromised credentials to exfiltrate data from SharePoint.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1530","text":"HAFNIUM has exfitrated data from OneDrive.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/"}]},{"id":"T1560.001","text":"HAFNIUM has used 7-Zip and WinRAR to compress stolen files for exfiltration.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"},{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/"}]},{"id":"T1071.001","text":"HAFNIUM has used open-source C2 frameworks, including Covenant.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"}]},{"id":"T1095","text":"HAFNIUM has used TCP for C2.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"}]},{"id":"T1105","text":"HAFNIUM has downloaded malware and tools--including Nishang and PowerCat--onto a compromised host.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"},{"name":"Rapid7 HAFNIUM Mar 2021","url":"https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2021/03/23/defending-against-the-zero-day-analyzing-attacker-behavior-post-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange/"}]},{"id":"T1132.001","text":"HAFNIUM has used ASCII encoding for C2 traffic.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"}]},{"id":"T1567.002","text":"HAFNIUM has exfiltrated data to file sharing sites, including MEGA.","cites":[{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/"}]}],"observables":[{"kind":"lolbin","value":"whoami","tech":"T1033"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"cmd.exe","tech":"T1059.003"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"tasklist","tech":"T1057"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"procdump","tech":"T1003.001"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"rundll32","tech":"T1218.011"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"ping","tech":"T1016.001"}],"sources":[{"name":"Volexity Exchange Marauder March 2021","url":"https://www.volexity.com/blog/2021/03/02/active-exploitation-of-microsoft-exchange-zero-day-vulnerabilities/","desc":"Gruzweig, J. et al. (2021, March 2). Operation Exchange Marauder: Active Exploitation of Multiple Zero-Day Microsoft Exchange Vulnerabilities. Retrieved March 3, 2021."},{"name":"Microsoft Threat Actor Naming July 2023","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365/security/intelligence/microsoft-threat-actor-naming?view=o365-worldwide","desc":"Microsoft . (2023, July 12). How Microsoft names threat actors. Retrieved November 17, 2023."},{"name":"Microsoft Silk Typhoon MAR 2025","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/03/05/silk-typhoon-targeting-it-supply-chain/","desc":"Microsoft Threat Intelligence . (2025, March 5). Silk Typhoon targeting IT supply chain. Retrieved March 20, 2025."},{"name":"Microsoft HAFNIUM March 2020","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/02/hafnium-targeting-exchange-servers/","desc":"MSTIC. (2021, March 2). HAFNIUM targeting Exchange Servers with 0-day exploits. Retrieved March 3, 2021."}],"softwareLinks":[{"id":"S0073","n":"ASPXSpy","t":"malware","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0073/"},{"id":"S0020","n":"China Chopper","t":"malware","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0020/"},{"id":"S1155","n":"Covenant","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1155/"},{"id":"S0357","n":"Impacket","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0357/"},{"id":"S0029","n":"PsExec","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0029/"},{"id":"S1011","n":"Tarrask","t":"malware","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1011/"}]}